### Configuring DOM Environment in vitest.config.ts

Source: https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v4.1.6/docs/guide/features.md

Set the `environment` option in your Vitest configuration to specify the DOM environment (e.g., 'happy-dom' or 'jsdom') for your tests.

```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config'

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    environment: 'happy-dom', // or 'jsdom', 'node'
  },
})
```

--------------------------------

### Configure environmentOptions for jsdom and happyDOM in Vitest

Source: https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v4.1.6/docs/config/environmentoptions.md

Use `environmentOptions` to provide specific settings for different test environments. Options are scoped by environment key, allowing distinct configurations for `jsdom` and `happyDOM` within the same project.

```js
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config'

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    environmentOptions: {
      jsdom: {
        url: 'http://localhost:3000',
      },
      happyDOM: {
        width: 300,
        height: 400,
      },
    },
  },
})
```

--------------------------------

### Specify Test Environment for a File with Control Comment

Source: https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v4.1.6/docs/guide/environment.md

Use a control comment at the top of a test file to set a specific environment, overriding the global configuration. This example sets the `jsdom` environment for the file.

```ts
// @vitest-environment jsdom

import { expect, test } from 'vitest'

test('test', () => {
  expect(typeof window).not.toBe('undefined')
})
```

--------------------------------

### Installing DOM Environments for Vitest

Source: https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v4.1.6/docs/guide/features.md

Install either happy-dom or jsdom to enable DOM and browser API mocking in Vitest tests.

```bash
$ npm i -D happy-dom
```

```bash
$ npm i -D jsdom
```

--------------------------------

### Configure TypeScript for jsdom environment

Source: https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/v4.1.6/docs/config/environment.md

Add vitest/jsdom to the types compiler option in tsconfig.json to enable TypeScript recognition of the jsdom global variable.

```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["vitest/jsdom"]
  }
}
```

